!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
! Absorption cross-section for H2SO4 : H2SO4 + hv-> SO3 + H2O
! New process implemented for CIFS-CB05BASCOE-GLOMAP (project CAMS-43, Graham Mann and Vincent.Huijnen)
! 118.3-180.2nm: Lane & Kjaergaard, J.Phys.Chem.A, 2008, fig.5:
!                - value at Ly-a copied manually from text. NOTE: 6.0e-17 from abstract gives same J
!                - values at other UV wl have actually negligible impact.
!                  They were obtained by digitization of fig.5, conversions (see crs_h2so4.xls)
!                  and interp to TUV_MIDATM wl grid using ch_wlgrid_crs.py 
! Visible:     Feierabend et al. (Chem.Phys.Lett.,2006); 
!                 3 bands in the visible (v=4,5,6) fitted into 3 matching wl bins 
!                 Unit conversions are briefly explained in comments after each wl bin; see crs_h2so4.xls
!                 Note: v=4 actually falls out of the our wl grid, was approx into last wl bin.
! WARNING: Photolysis in the visible MUST be reduced due to quenching : see
!           Miller, Gerber, and Vaida (GRL,2007); implementation thru pressure-dependent quantum yields
!           is done in routine CALC_QYTP and explained in crs_h2so4.xls
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
